android: take java.io.tmpdir from TMPDIR

java_props_md.c sets sprops.tmp_dir to P_tmpdir and only MacOSX gets a
per-user directory; TMPDIR is not consulted on Linux, so java.io.tmpdir is
always /tmp. On Android /tmp exists but belongs to the shell user (mode
0771), so no application may write there and every File.createTempFile()
fails with EACCES. That is what stops the build tools, e.g.

  javax.imageio.IIOException: Can't create cache file!
  Caused by: java.nio.file.AccessDeniedException: /tmp/imageio....tmp

  at build.tools.icondata.awt.ToBin.main(ToBin.java:35)

and it hits every program that needs a scratch file, so honour TMPDIR when
it is set. When it is not set the behaviour is unchanged.

diff --git a/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/lang/java_props_md.c b/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/lang/java_props_md.c
--- a/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/lang/java_props_md.c
+++ b/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/lang/java_props_md.c
@@ -395,6 +395,14 @@
 
     /* tmp dir */
     sprops.tmp_dir = P_tmpdir;
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+    /* /tmp belongs to the shell user on Android, so it is not writable by
+     * an application; TMPDIR is where the environment says temp files go. */
+    v = getenv("TMPDIR");
+    if (v != NULL && v[0] != '\0') {
+        sprops.tmp_dir = v;
+    }
+#endif
 #ifdef MACOSX
     /* darwin has a per-user temp dir */
     static char tmp_path[PATH_MAX];
